  "names": {
    "en": "Final Fantasy X / X-2 HD Remaster",
    "ja": "ファイナルファンタジーX/X-2 HDリマスター"
  },
  "summaries": {
    "en": "Complete HD Remaster guide for FFX/X-2—Sphere Grid optimization, Blitzball mastery, and Penance preparation.",
    "ja": "FFX/X-2 HDリマスター完全攻略。スフィア盤最適化、ブリッツボール制覇、ペナンス撃破準備を徹底解説。"
  },
  "category": "jrpg",
  "difficulty": "intermediate",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "The Sphere Grid is the core character advancement system—use Expert Grid to allow all characters to access any sphere path freely, or Standard Grid for structured learning.",
      "Overdrives are charged by specific conditions per character (Tidus by time passing, Auron by taking damage, Lulu by taking hits); trigger the matching condition before entering boss fights to preload Overdrive.",
      "Aeon Overdrives can be accumulated off-screen; rotate Aeons in and out of battle to charge all Overdrive gauges simultaneously, providing emergency boss burst damage.",
      "Blitzball is optional but rewarding—recruiting Wakka's Reels from tournament rewards is the primary source of his best Overdrive reels; play tournaments regularly through early mid-game.",
      "For FFX-2, the Job System (Dressphere) benefits from early investment in the Trainer and Alchemist Dresspheres as AP income multipliers for the rest of the dressphere grid."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "スフィア盤がキャラクター成長のコアシステム。エキスパートグリッドは全キャラクターが自由にどのスフィアパスにもアクセス可能。標準グリッドは体系的な学習向け。",
      "オーバードライブはキャラクターごとの固有条件でチャージされる（ティーダは時間経過、アーロンはダメージ受け、ルールーはヒット受け）。ボス戦前に対応する条件を発動してオーバードライブを予充填する。",
      "召喚獣のオーバードライブはオフスクリーンで蓄積可能。召喚獣を交互に呼んで全オーバードライブゲージを同時にチャージし、緊急ボスバーストダメージを確保する。",
      "ブリッツボールは任意だが価値がある。ワッカのリールをトーナメント報酬から集めることが最良のオーバードライブリールの主な入手経路。序盤〜中盤を通じて定期的にトーナメントに参加する。",
      "FFX-2では、ジョブシステム（ドレスフィア）が序盤のトレーナーとアルケミストへの投資で残りのドレスフィアグリッド全体のAPインカム乗数として機能する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Sphere Grid Route Planning",
        "body": "In Expert Sphere Grid mode, the optimal path routes each character to their specialized stats first, then branches toward support stats after initial specialization is complete. Tidus: prioritize Agility and Strength nodes. Yuna: prioritize MP and Magic nodes before reaching Lulu's segment for Black Magic. Auron: maximize Strength and Defense before extending toward Auron's own path end. Lulu and Wakka have complete paths that should not be branched from until their own paths are fully traversed."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Preparation for the Monster Arena",
        "body": "The Monster Arena in Calm Lands (available from Chapter 5 onward) is the primary source of late-game equipment and is required for the Celestial Weapons. Capturing 10 of each monster type in each region completes regional fiends; completion rewards include items needed for Celestial Weapon upgrades. Systematically capture fiends in every region during story progression rather than returning after the story ends."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Penance and Dark Aeon Preparation",
        "body": "The PS4/Steam version of FFX HD includes the International/PAL content including Dark Aeons and Penance—the hardest optional fights in the game. Penance has 12 million HP and requires characters with 9,999 HP, 99,999 MP, 255 Strength, 255 Defense, and maxed Agility. The only efficient path to these stats is fully traversing the Sphere Grid and obtaining armor with Auto-Haste, Auto-Phoenix, and Ribbon (or Stoneproof) abilities."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Not activating Celestial Weapon crests and sigils—Celestial Weapons without the crest/sigil deal severely reduced damage (sometimes less than basic weapons); they only become dominant after full activation.",
      "Skipping Blitzball until late game—Wakka's Attack Reels (the strongest Overdrive in the game for single-target damage) can only be obtained via Blitzball tournament prizes; skipping Blitzball delays the strongest DPS tool significantly.",
      "Using regular saves at key points without using Clear Sphere saves—Save Spheres allow you to retry boss fights, but quitting back to the title screen from a regular checkpoint before a boss can miss the save sphere opportunity.",
      "Not using Auto-Life or Life Spell reactively during difficult boss phases—several late-game bosses hit multiple characters simultaneously; having Auto-Life pre-cast prevents full party KO.",
      "Mixing physical and magic damage builds on the same character in Sphere Grid—split builds dilute both stats; commit each character to either physical (STR) or magic (MAG) focused path."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "天地創造武器の紋章とシジルを発動させない。紋章/シジルなしの天地創造武器は極めて少ないダメージ（時に基本武器以下）しか与えない。完全発動後のみ強力になる。",
      "ブリッツボールを後半まで後回しにする。ワッカのアタックリール（単体ダメージで最強のオーバードライブ）はブリッツボールトーナメント賞品からしか入手不可。スキップすると最強DPSツールが大幅に遅れる。",
      "重要ポイントでセーブ球を使わずに通常セーブをする。セーブ球でボス再戦が可能。ボス前の通常チェックポイントからタイトルに戻るとセーブ球の機会を逃す可能性がある。",
      "困難なボスフェーズでオートライフや蘇生魔法を反応的に使わない。後半ボスは複数キャラクターを同時に攻撃する。オートライフを事前に付与することでパーティ全滅を防げる。",
      "スフィア盤で同じキャラクターに物理と魔法ダメージビルドを混在させる。分割ビルドは両方のステータスを薄める。各キャラクターを物理（STR）か魔法（MAG）どちらかに特化させる。"
    ]
  },
